[statement]
A package whose condition never holds, since nothing provides `zz`, has
its dependencies chosen for where the walk reaches it, and those choices
reserve what they hold. `r` needs `F`, reached through `r` before `z`;
`f1`, chosen for it, holds `K`. `S`, decided first, passes over `s1`,
which would hold `K` too, for `f2`, which then answers `F` as well.
Contrast
`a-condition-that-never-holds-reserves-a-provider-only-if-required`.

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:n z

P:n
V:1

P:z
V:1
D:S F

P:r
V:1
i:n zz
D:F

P:f1
V:1
k:100
p:F K=1

P:f2
V:1
k:10
p:F S

P:s1
V:1
k:100
p:S K=1

P:s2
V:1
k:10
p:S

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install n 1
install f2 1
install z 1
install top 1
